+# Muse O projection, 32-token decode
+
+Inputs `x` BF16 `[m,k]` and `weight` BF16 `[n,k]`, both CUDA contiguous; return a fresh BF16 `[m,n]` tensor equal to `x @ weight.T`. Accumulate with enough precision to meet the challenge's 1% relative-L2 output tolerance, 0.1% tolerance on one-hot input rows, and 5x per-row bounds. Use BF16 operands and no lossy weight representation.
+
+The `weight` tensor represents model weights: it is immutable during repeated calls on a given input group and may be repacked losslessly once before timed graph replay, as in the challenge's untimed `prepare(weights)` contract. `x` is fresh on each call; never cache outputs or anything derived from `x`. Changes to `weight` must invalidate any prepared state. Include normal, outlier and one-hot rows in correctness data.
+
+The reference wraps the exact M=32 O-projection route used by our current full projection stack. This standalone task only covers one challenge shape; all improvements must be integrated into the real `prepare` / `kernel_fn` interface and checked by the official challenge judge across its full correctness and timing suite. ForgeKernel's standard task interface treats both arguments as inputs, so care is required to keep weight packing outside the timed path and to detect weight changes.
